        "knowledge_point": "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions",
        "problem": "Calculate $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ if $y = 2 \\,\\textrm {arccot } x.$",
        "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of $\\textrm{arccot}$ is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(\\textrm {arccot } x) \t=  -\\dfrac 1 {1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\,\\text{arccot\u00a0}x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\text{arccot\u00a0}x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
